# Choosing the right collection

## Step 1 — access shape → interface

- Sequence / index / order / duplicates → **`List`**
- Membership / uniqueness → **`Set`**
- Look up by key → **`Map`**
- Process in order (FIFO / stack / priority) → **`Deque` / `PriorityQueue`**

## Step 2 — ordering → implementation

- No order → **`HashSet` / `HashMap`** (fast default)
- Insertion order → **`LinkedHashSet` / `LinkedHashMap`**
- Sorted / ranges → **`TreeSet` / `TreeMap`** (O(log n))

## Defaults, in one breath

**List → `ArrayList` · Set → `HashSet` · Map → `HashMap` · Queue/Stack → `ArrayDeque`** · priority → `PriorityQueue` · enum keys → `EnumMap`/`EnumSet`

## Don't forget

- Program to the **interface**; prefer **immutable** + copy at boundaries; value types as **records**, **immutable keys**
